# CLI

Every entry node includes an interactive command-line interface for direct access to the node state. The CLI is automatically disabled when stdin is not a terminal (e.g., in Docker or when running as a daemon).

## Commands

| Command | Aliases | Description |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| `ping` | `p` | Show version and uptime |
| `stats` | `s` | Display traffic statistics |
| `peers` | - | List connected peers |
| `sessions` | `t`, `tuns` | List active exit node sessions |
| `route add <cidr>` | - | Add a network route |
| `route del <cidr>` | `route rm` | Remove a network route |
| `disconnect <id>` | `kick`, `kill` | Disconnect a peer |
| `help` | `?` | Show available commands |
| `quit` | `q`, `exit` | Exit the application |

## Example Session

```
wallhack> stats
Traffic Statistics:
  Bytes In:     1.23 MB
  Bytes Out:    456.78 KB

wallhack> route add 10.0.0.0/8
Route added: 10.0.0.0/8
```
